      "refersTo": "rehearsal-panel",
      "description": "The dark two-part enclosure and typography of the interactive rehearsal. This excerpt shows its visual shell, not the running demo.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-rehearsal\"><div class=\"ds-display\"><span class=\"ds-demo-label\"><i></i>Rehearsal <small>Interactive demo</small></span><p class=\"ds-script\">You don’t need to memorize every word.</p><p class=\"ds-script\">You just need a little room to be yourself.</p></div><div class=\"ds-controls\"><h3>Your pace.<br>Your voice.</h3><p>Keep your place without learning every line by heart.</p><span class=\"ds-note\">Browser demo. Your camera stays off.</span></div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-rehearsal{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr;border-radius:var(--radius-panel,24px);background:#17161d;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 28px 80px -35px rgba(0,0,0,.6);font-family:var(--font-sans,Figtree,sans-serif);color:var(--color-text,#fff)}.ds-display{padding:28px;background:linear-gradient(130deg,#282135,#18161f)}.ds-demo-label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:12px;color:#e9dff7;font-weight:600}.ds-demo-label i{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--color-lavender,#c3aaff)}.ds-demo-label small{margin-left:auto;color:#bfb5ce;font-size:12px;font-weight:400}.ds-script{font-size:32px;line-height:1.45;letter-spacing:-.6px;font-weight:600;color:#e7ddef;margin:24px 0}.ds-controls{padding:42px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px}.ds-controls h3{font-size:32px;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.7px;margin:0}.ds-controls p{font-size:17px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--color-muted,rgba(255,255,255,.75));margin:0}.ds-note{font-size:12px;color:var(--color-quiet,#a6a3ad);line-height:1.5}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Aspect Ratio Chips",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "format-chip",
      "description": "Selected and idle format buttons from the illustrative crop preview.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-formats\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Preview video aspect ratio\"><button type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"true\">9:16</button><button type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">1:1</button><button type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">16:9</button><button type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">4:5</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-formats{display:flex;gap:8px}.ds-formats button{border:0;background:#27232f;color:var(--color-muted,rgba(255,255,255,.75));padding:10px 15px;border-radius:30px;font:400 14px/1.5 var(--font-sans,Figtree,sans-serif);min-height:44px;cursor:pointer}.ds-formats button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#6241ab;color:#fff}.ds-formats button:hover{background:#4c376c}.ds-formats button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-lavender,#c3aaff);outline-offset:6px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "FAQ Disclosure",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "faq-disclosure",
      "description": "A native disclosure with a hairline divider, lavender open state, and rotating caret.",
      "html": "<details class=\"ds-faq\"><summary>Do I need an account?<svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 256\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z\"/></svg></summary><p>No account is required. Your scripts and recordings are stored locally.</p></details>",
      "css": ".ds-faq{border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule,rgba(255,255,255,.12));font-family:var(--font-sans,Figtree,sans-serif);color:var(--color-text,#fff);max-width:640px}.ds-faq summary{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:22px 0;list-style:none;cursor:pointer;font-size:18px;line-height:1.4;font-weight:500}.ds-faq summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.ds-faq summary svg{color:var(--color-quiet,#a6a3ad);transition:transform .2s}.ds-faq[open] summary{color:var(--color-lavender,#c3aaff)}.ds-faq[open] summary svg{transform:rotate(180deg)}.ds-faq summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-lavender,#c3aaff);outline-offset:6px}.ds-faq p{padding:0 28px 24px 0;margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--color-muted,rgba(255,255,255,.75))}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-faq summary svg{transition:none}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Rehearsal Stage",
    "overview": "The Rehearsal Stage places luminous words and recognizable iPhone screens on a near-black canvas. The owner selected Detail’s measured visual language: Figtree, lavender-white display type, violet gradient pills, broad section spacing, and device-led compositions. The result is direct, spacious, and lightly theatrical, with the approved lavender ring icon retaining the app’s identity.\n\nDepth comes from a restrained combination of dark tonal panels, device shadows, and violet light. The handwritten QR annotation adds one informal voice beside precise sans-serif type. Controls feel rounded and tactile; supporting labels stay quiet so the words, product imagery, and actions carry the hierarchy.\n\nThis specification belongs only to the Astro marketing site in Marketing/. It does not replace the native iPhone app’s design tokens or the parent project’s design documentation. Preserve the approved app icon and the actual native UI shown in screenshots.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Near-black canvas with lavender-white display type and violet accents.",
      "Large Figtree headings, quiet explanatory copy, and open vertical rhythm.",
      "Rounded gradient actions, dark demonstration panels, and phone silhouettes.",
      "Caveat reserved for the QR annotation; native system type reserved for illustrative app chrome."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Violet Action Rule",
        "body": "Use the violet gradient for prominent actions and lavender for quiet links, focus, and selected details. Keep dark surfaces dominant.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Three Voices Rule",
        "body": "Use Figtree for marketing, Caveat for the QR annotation, and the system stack for illustrative app UI. Preserve typography inside actual screenshots.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Local Light Rule",
        "body": "Concentrate glow on the display heading and device stage. Keep reading panels and supporting text clear rather than adding a glow to every surface.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the approved lavender ring app icon and the native screenshots’ original UI.",
      "Do use the code’s responsive typography and container overrides when extending the marketing site.",
      "Do keep keyboard focus visible and preserve the reduced-motion treatment.",
      "Do label actual app screenshots and illustrative previews honestly.",
      "Do keep the CTA and QR code bound to the same destination in src/data/site.ts."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don’t apply this marketing specification to the parent native app or replace its tokens.",
      "Don’t replace the owner’s pinned Detail direction with another visual world.",
      "Don’t use Caveat for navigation, long copy, or primary actions.",
      "Don’t crop away the meaningful app content when adapting device compositions.",
      "Don’t present the illustrative camera, editing, browser rehearsal, or format preview as an actual app screenshot."
    ]
  }
}
